  "notes": [
    "Chaos run: Every worker is replaced in turn, one at a time: the mock announces draining and keeps serving for a period above the heartbeat plus the registry refresh, then refuses and finishes what is in flight; the agent deregisters; a fresh worker takes its place.",
    "What this embedded mock cluster cannot show here: Process signals: the harness calls the same drain path a SIGTERM takes (mock drain and agent.Shutdown) in process. It tells the registry at once instead of through the next probe, so the announce period only has to cover the gateway's refresh. A real preStop is Phase 17.",
    "Windows follow when the fault was really applied and cleared. Gateway counters (attempts per request, retries) are read at the tick that opens and closes a window (every 1s), so an attempt of a request in flight at a boundary falls in the next window; the per-request figures come from the clients.",
    "Closed-loop clients: 14 for the whole run on 32 request slots (24 left serving). Closed-loop clients wait for each response, so a failing worker also slows the offered load.",
    "Load average (1, 5 and 15 minutes) at the start of the run: 4.10 4.49 4.42; at the end: 4.44 4.56 4.45."
  ],
